From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:33:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] settings: tips that lead to a row Advanced settings hides
 stay away while it is off

With Settings > Advanced settings off (0107), a tip whose only point is a
hidden row isn't shown: the Extended memory notice (posted once the switch
is turned on; Kiln keeps it pending), the boot loader notices (a new gate:
they wait, unmarked, and show at the next look once it is on), the new
plugin toasts, the firmware update notice (posted by the first check with
it on) and the tour's home-editing step. Problems stay shown and say how
to get there: the internal error toast's debug bundle, a full disk's
Storage, a rejected or missing API key and the Z Offset by Material
warning add "(turn on Settings > Advanced settings first)" or "(shown with
Settings > Advanced settings on)", as does the telemetry explanation's
View Telemetry Data. One text serves both modes. English, English (UK,
empty) and Russian strings.

Shortcuts to a page it hides do nothing while it is off, the item kept
as read-only information: the Printer page's Filament Sensors, Width
Sensors, Retraction and Power chips (not clickable, so no press effect),
Controls' "N more sensors" link (it keeps its tap, so the tap doesn't
reach the temperature card behind it), the filament sensor tile's tap to
the sensor settings, and HelixScreen's update banner (it observes the
setting: hidden at once when it is turned off, back when it is turned
on; not dismissed).
